==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|nobilite}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|nobilitas}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/noʊˈbɪlɨti/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|nobilities}}

# A [[noble]] or privileged social class, historically accompanied by a [[hereditary]] title; [[aristocracy]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The quality of being [[noble]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|noble or privileged social class}} {{l|en|aristocracy}}, {{l|en|upper class}}
* {{sense|quality of being noble}} {{l|en|nobleness}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|noble or privileged social class}} {{l|en|plebeian}}
* {{sense|quality of being noble}} {{l|en|meanness}}, {{l|en|ignobility}}

